nodecode-interim-ledger is a rewrite of olric3015's olric3015/hermes-plugins:

  https://github.com/olric3015/hermes-plugins
  commit ed94f43f5573b4b55f355bb97f37c225e36d6f19

MIT License, Copyright (c) 2026 olric3015 (LICENSE)

What was rewritten: the plugin's one job - keep a row for every message a model
writes in the middle of a turn, beside a tool call, and answer /interim-log with
which models write them, in how many turns, how many a turn gets, their median
length and when the last one was - as a Nodecode cell. Its row shape (the
timestamp, a 12-digit SHA-256 of the session and of the turn, the model, the
provider, the step of the turn, the length of the message; never the text and
never the ids), its JSON-lines file under the home, its trim to the newest rows
past the section's bound, its options (/interim-log session | all | Nh | Nd |
providers | days | recent [N] | clear, its one-line refusal of an option it
does not know, and its rule that a window word titles the report) and its two
reports carry over. Where the plugin subscribed to Hermes's on_interim_message
hook, the cell advises NLK:RECORD-ASSISTANT-MESSAGE -- the one function every
completed provider round of every turn passes through -- and records a row when
the message carried text beside at least one tool call, which is the same
message Hermes fired its hook for. A final answer with no calls leaves no row,
as it did there. It still only watches: an error in the observer is swallowed,
so a round records itself exactly as it would without the cell. The three
reports are on the manual as interim-ledger:summary, interim-ledger:recent and
interim-ledger:clear for a report taken through eval.

What was left out, and why: Hermes's surface column (telegram, discord, cli)
and its streamed flag are gone, because Nodecode records no per-turn surface
and no per-message "already streamed" fact: a turn reaches the cell as a turn,
whatever room or shell asked for it. The column Hermes spent on the surface is
the number of tool calls the message rode instead, which the wire message
carries and which says something a reader can use. The setting is a row count
rather than the plugin's 2 MB byte bound, since one row's size no longer varies
with a room's name. The plugin's own card image, its pytest suite and its
end-to-end harness are not part of the cell.
